/** A claim whose due is above the proof threshold in force on its date was settled or approved with no proof. */
public class ClaimProofNeededException extends Exception {

    public ClaimProofNeededException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}
# PUT /api/sheets/{sheetId}/claims/{claimId}/status/{status} — move a claim to OPEN, SETTLED or VOID.
# DRAFT -> OPEN -> SETTLED, and DRAFT, OPEN or PENDING -> VOID; a steward may also void a SETTLED claim within 7 days
# of its settlement (the status log's SETTLED date) by the sheet's today. A clerk settling a claim above the clerk limit
# makes it PENDING; from PENDING a steward (not its opener) approves it (SETTLED) or rejects it (OPEN, with a
# "reason" in the body). Any other change is refused with 409 and nothing is stored. 404 for a claim not on the
# sheet; 422 for a claim dated inside a closed period, or for a settle or approve of a claim with no proof whose due is
# above the proof threshold in force on its date.
